+// The first cut counted one branch -- `hasInvalidKeyAtIndex` -- and there are
+// five ways out of that function that discard a frame: the SIF-reject arm, a
+// missing key set, a decrypt that throws a CryptorError, a decrypt that throws
+// anything ELSE (an AV1 payload makes `getUnencryptedBytes` throw a plain
